course: dictionary
lesson: 10209
title: One word, three meanings: tired
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word tired can mean different things. The words around it show you which meaning is right. «Tired eyes are a sign that you need rest and sleep.» Here tired means your body needs rest, because the sentence tells you what to do about it.
explain: Tired can also mean bored or annoyed with something that has gone on too long. Look for the clue word «of» after it, as in «sick and tired of waiting». The word of tells you that tired is about how you feel about something, not about sleep.
explain: A third meaning is less common: old and used too much, as in «tired old shoes». When you meet tired, try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
fact: «Tired» means needing rest or sleep because you have used a lot of energy.
fact: «Tired of» something means bored or annoyed with it because it has gone on too long.
fact: «Tired» can also mean old and used too much, as in «tired old shoes», but this is less common.
fact: Children need about 9 to 12 hours of sleep a night, so feeling tired in the day is a sign to rest.
fact: Tired people make mistakes, so it is wise to rest before a long trip.
exercise: «Binge-watching a whole series in one weekend can make you feel tired and strange the next day.» Here tired means | Old and worn out | *Needing rest and sleep | Bored of the show | Very happy
exercise: Mia says, «I am tired of waiting for the bus.» What does tired mean here? | Full of energy and ready to run | Asleep on the seat | Old and used too much | *Bored or annoyed because it has gone on too long
exercise: Which phrase shows the shoes are old and used too much? | Shoes that fit well | *Tired old shoes | Shoes on the shelf | Bright new shoes
test: «Tired eyes are a sign that you need rest and sleep.» What does tired mean here? | Old and used too much | Bored of looking at things | Happy and bright | *Needing rest or sleep
test: Sam says, «I am sick and tired of this game.» What does tired mean? | Happy with the game | Sleepy from playing | *Bored or annoyed with the game, which has gone on too long | Old and worn out
exam: Which sentence uses tired to mean needing sleep? | Tired old boots by the door | I am tired of the rain | *Screens before bed can make you tired the next day | She is tired of waiting
